msgstr ""

#: 6477e0bda303417f8daa7360c767c7a5 atomate2.siesta.flows.neb:1 of
msgid "NEB (Nudged Elastic Band) workflow implementations."
msgstr ""

#: 667d8416cc4247ba96a26b122080a0ac atomate2.siesta.flows.neb:3 of
msgid "This package provides three types of NEB workflows:"
msgstr ""

#: atomate2.siesta.flows.neb:5 ecbb0769a4c24b32baa73eb66d987046 of
msgid ""
"**AseNebFlowMaker**: Full ASE-based NEB with Python optimization - Uses "
"optimizers (PER_IMAGE_LBFGS/FIRE/BFGS) with SIESTA as calculator - "
"Persistent folder approach (custodian-style) - Default: PER_IMAGE_LBFGS "
"(each image has its own L-BFGS, like Lua FLOS) - Best for: Complex "
"reaction paths, climbing image NEB"
msgstr ""

#: 2069278339cc46ba8a2c546d2b959d19 atomate2.siesta.flows.neb:11 of
msgid ""
"**NebDirectFlowMaker**: FLOS/Lua-based NEB from two structures - Uses "
"SIESTA's Lua scripting (neb.lua) - Simpler setup, runs entirely within "
"SIESTA - Best for: Quick NEB calculations, SIESTA-native workflows"
msgstr ""

#: atomate2.siesta.flows.neb:16 de2a2aeebf394e4ab3fb7eb5f20c8b35 of
msgid ""
"**NebVacancyExchangeFlowMaker**: Specialized for atom swapping - "
"Generates initial/final by swapping two atoms - Uses FLOS/Lua NEB - Best "
"for: Vacancy diffusion, atom exchange barriers"
msgstr ""

#: atomate2.siesta.flows.neb:22 ccb6559efae24007a66df33df64a62ee of
msgid "Available Optimizers (AseNebFlowMaker)"
msgstr ""

#: 19f0a51c9d7e454c90d3d8a5864670fc atomate2.siesta.flows.neb:23
#: atomate2.siesta.flows.neb.ase_neb.AseNebFlowMaker:65
#: f02d9163e9a74472a6dcd2f544638289 of
msgid "**Per-image optimizers** (recommended - like Lua FLOS):"
msgstr ""

#: 7de23a1a88684c4fbb32b940c3c32c8f atomate2.siesta.flows.neb:25 of
msgid ""
"**PER_IMAGE_LBFGS** (default): Each NEB image has its own L-BFGS "
"optimizer with limited memory (~20 steps). Best balance of convergence "
"and memory."
msgstr ""

#: 2664cab6bb394695b444857f08cfa817 4122f7d298d542ca80246c8dde54becb
#: atomate2.siesta.flows.neb:28
#: atomate2.siesta.flows.neb.ase_neb.AseNebFlowMaker:71 of
msgid ""
"**PER_IMAGE_BFGS**: Each NEB image has its own full BFGS optimizer with "
"complete inverse Hessian. May converge faster for small systems but uses "
"more memory (O(n²) per image)."
msgstr ""

#: 037d2d110a2c48c0a371f22bf92c8a39 56b2f9a08754487f89dfaf4ee639d3c0
#: atomate2.siesta.flows.neb:32
#: atomate2.siesta.flows.neb.ase_neb.AseNebFlowMaker:75 of
msgid "**Global optimizers** (treat all images together):"
msgstr ""

#: 6616fe687d16471da9e2da99a8ab1546 atomate2.siesta.flows.neb:34 of
msgid "**FIRE**: No Hessian, handles oscillations well. Good fallback option."
msgstr ""

#: 0bab459a6d5c421f838d556f86562e87 atomate2.siesta.flows.neb:36 of
msgid ""
"**LBFGS/BFGS**: Global optimizer for all images combined. Can oscillate "
"due to mixing curvature information from different regions."
msgstr ""

#: 35ea37602bf6432fb82ff637f3c7175f
#: atomate2.siesta.flows.neb.ase_neb.AseNebFlowMaker:1 of
msgid ""
"Jobflow maker to run NEB calculations using ASE optimizer with persistent"
" folders."
msgstr ""

#: atomate2.siesta.flows.neb.ase_neb.AseNebFlowMaker:3
#: dfbc8f880458422eb2313b76876134b6 of
msgid ""
"This maker uses ASE's NEB implementation with SIESTA as the calculator, "
"instead of SIESTA's Lua scripting. This approach is: - More portable (no "
"FLOS/Lua required) - Easier to customize (Python-based) - Better for "
"advanced NEB methods (climbing image, string methods) - Optimized with "
"persistent folders (custodian-style approach)"
